FRONT B2 (r67 Thm 9.1 explicit pi) -- hand proof of the general no-go for finitely presented pi
==========================================================================================
Agent: FRONT-B2.  Date: 2026-08-16.  Every inequality below is explicit; every step is
re-checked numerically/exactly by source/frontB2_proofcheck.py (output at the end of this file).

Setting (r67 eq 9.2/9.3).  X = N \ {1,2}.  For m >= 3
    (P pi)(m) = pi(2m) + [m = 2 mod 3] pi((2m-1)/3),          pi = 0 on {1,2}.
Target: pi > 0 on X, pi in l^1, P pi <= pi on X.  Both predecessors of m lie in X for m >= 3
(2m >= 6; (2m-1)/3 = 1 only for m = 2), so for m >= 3 every summand of (P pi)(m) is a genuine
positive term.

Lemma 0 (edge monotonicity, r67 eq 9.4).  If P pi <= pi and n >= 3, T(n) >= 3, then
    pi(n) <= (P pi)(T n) <= pi(T n).                                                     (0.1)
Moreover the inequality is STRICT whenever n is odd: T n = m has BOTH predecessors n = (2m-1)/3
and 2m in X, so  pi(n) + pi(2m) <= pi(m)  and pi(2m) > 0 gives  pi(n) < pi(m).          (0.2)
(For n even, n = 2m, the inequality pi(2m) <= pi(m) may be an equality only if m != 2 mod 3.)

